PATCH NOTICE
  Twenty-three literal string replacements were applied to marked.esm.js, by a patcher that
  throws when a pattern is missing or occurs more than once. Every guard is a necessary
  condition for the anchored regex it precedes, so the rendered HTML is unchanged.

    inline loop   declare `c=e.charCodeAt(0)` once per iteration; guard escape, tag, link,
                  reflink, emStrong, codespan, br, del and autolink on that character; guard
                  url on urlStart(c,e); splice urlStart in before `function Ie(a){`
    block loop    declare b0 (first non-space char, up to three leading spaces), bn (a
                  newline exists after index 0), bc (b0 is space or tab), bl (b0 can start a
                  list marker); guard fences, heading, hr, blockquote, html, def, table,
                  lheading, code and list

  No regex, renderer, token shape or parser code was modified. To re-verify, fetch the
  pristine file (sha256 above) and diff it against this one.
